 "notes": "SOLA (South Louisiana Center for the Arts) has NO fascia lettering: the curved black textured-stucco band above (the old Sound Shop front) is blank. Its sign is a multicolour vinyl decal on the black glass vestibule panel: a white contour backing with 'S' lime, 'O' a magenta disc with white comedy/tragedy masks, 'L' blue, 'A' orange with a white treble clef, then 'SOUTH LOUISIANA' and 'CENTER FOR THE ARTS' in white heavy sans (Lilita One, condensed). Traced from the contact-sheet tile (the only frame with the whole logo; soft, so edges are smoothed and the mask faces are blobs); the right edge of the white backing is clipped by the squared-up frame by a few cm. The builder can't put it on the glass: mount_y -1.6 drops it from the fascia toward window height; better placed on the storefront glass by hand. Size a guess (~1.6 m wide) from the ~2.5 m glass panel. An older projecting black panel sign (round orange/yellow logo) is glimpsed far away in IMG_4419 only; not modelled.",
 "mount": "glass",
 "glass_y": 0.2
